Fixed #1087 (commit e1a63e3a): outside a git repo, yoyo grep hello a now finds the match in a single file.

Cause: outside a git repo, /grep runs plain grep -r. Given a single file instead of a directory, grep leaves the filename off its output (1:hello, or just 1 in count mode). My parser expects the filename on every line, so it threw them all away and said "No matches found." with exit 1. The context mode showed the line but put "0 matches" under it. -H is grep's flag for printing the filename in this exact case. git grep always prints it, which is why this never happened inside a repo.

Fix: I added -H to the three non-git grep commands (plain -rnH, count -rcH, context -rnH). Those three lines plus the line that loads the new test file are the only changes to src/commands_search.rs.

Tests are in the new src/commands_search_grep_h_tests.rs. Each one first checks that its temp directory is not inside a git repo; otherwise the git path would run and the test would prove nothing.
• Rows that were broken: a, ./a, note.txt, -c (gives a:1) and -C 1 (shows the context with a "1 match" footer). Four tests covered these and all four failed before the fix.
• Rows that must not change: a file with no match still prints "No matches found." in plain and count mode. A directory path and . give the same results as before the fix. Both near-miss tests passed before and after.
• Positive control: I removed -H from the plain command, ran the tests and put it back, all in one command. Exactly the two plain-command tests failed, by name, then went green again.
• Real binary: hello a now prints a:1: hello and exits 0; hello miss still prints "No matches found." and exits 1.

The format check, clippy with -D warnings, the build and the full test suite all pass. commands_search.rs is now 4586 lines against its registered 4573, which is inside the 50-line grace band, so I didn't change the size register.

Also in the commit:
• Left for later: yoyo grep hello a b still joins the two paths into one path a b. I checked the parser and it does join the extra words with a space. I filed this as #1091 before the push, so closing #1087 doesn't close the only place it was tracked.
• Docs: docs/src/usage/commands.md now says the non-git command is grep -rnH instead of grep -rn.
• Old `#1087` mentions: a search found none in user-facing text. The only mentions are the new code comments.
